  "step_3": "The decision reason focuses on the maximum magnitude outcome (highest absolute value) and its probability, preferring the lottery where this outcome is more favorable when weighted by probability. In contrast, the individual focuses on the possibility of avoiding any loss (the 0 Euro outcome in Lottery B with 20% probability), which is not the maximum magnitude outcome (that would be -4000). The individual does not reference the 4000 Euro loss as a key factor, nor do they compare the weighted impact of the most extreme losses. Instead, their reasoning is driven by the attractiveness of a zero outcome, which is a different cognitive mechanism—possibly reflecting probability weighting or aspiration-level thinking. There is no evidence that the individual considered the maximum magnitude outcome or applied a rule based on its favorability and probability. Therefore, the decision reason was not used in the deliberation.",
  "final_assessment_score": 10
