  "step_3": "The decision reason focuses on the maximum magnitude outcome (i.e., the highest possible gain) and its probability. The individual considers the highest outcomes in both lotteries (6000 vs. 4000) and explicitly prefers the higher amount despite lower or similar probabilities. They weigh the higher value more heavily than the probability, which aligns with the reason’s rule of favoring the more favorable maximum magnitude outcome weighted by probability—here, same probability but higher value. The individual’s focus on the highest gain and willingness to accept lower chances matches the core logic of the reason. Although the verbal report includes additional framing (e.g., no loss possible, subjective risk acceptance), the central justification—choosing based on the higher possible prize—is consistent with the decision reason. Therefore, the information considered and the justification align closely with the reason.",
  "final_assessment_score": 90
